					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I have been with this guild a long time. I remember some of the original members -- Caracarn, Ukari, Symbios, Salmissyra, and Goldeneyez. Back then Malcom (or Maelcum) was my only character and the guild was vibrant and and I was enraptured with it all. Then the summer came and many of the original members left. I spent weeks, literally weeks, where I would play as the only guild member online. Towards the end of the summer I finally saw Ukari on and he promised me the guild would restart and be great and that I should stick with it for a little longer. I met Coramor and he told me of the guild restructuring with Ukari as the new leader and Coramor as the co-leader. Many of you joined at this point and I was happy to see you all. I became an officer both with Malcom and Chumlee in the hopes that this would be a &quot;golden age&quot; for our guild. However, it seems that the cycle is happening again and all those &quot;dedicated&quot; members are jumping ship. The promises made to me by Ukari have not been delivered. I have been a member of this guild for nearly nine months and I have seen many good friends come and go because of political problems with this guild and I have seen little organization and structure accomplished. A guild is only as good as its members who will work together to make the guild stronger even in the face of adversity. This is not something I have seen consistently, and perhaps I have not done enough on my own part. For this I apologize. To those of you who I have become good friends with, I hope that you will keep in touch with me wherever you go. If you find a guild that does act on those qualities that are lacking here please let me know. For those of you who stay in PoTD, if a new guild does rise from the ashes of PoTD please let me know also. And to all of you, never hesitate to call on Chumlee, for my oath when I joined the guild as Malcom -- (yes there was a time when we were required to give a reason as to why we should be a full member) remains the same. &quot;I am Malcom. I may not be the fastest or the brightest, but I am big of heart and always loyal to those in need.&quot; I still plan to attend Dalnir and carry out the christmas exchange if any are interested. After that I will make my final decision to stay or leave.<br />
<br />
-- Strength and honor,<br />
Chumlee						</td>
